  "id": "COMPOUND:15175 - PROTEIN:1442",
  "verbalization": "The visible evidence strongly suggests a relationship between the compound (1R,6S,8R,11R)-3,8-dibromo-4,11,12,12-tetramethyl-7-oxatricyclo[6.3.1.01,6]dodeca-3,9-dien-11-ol and DNA polymerase alpha subunit B, as it is identified as a target of multiple compounds that act as activators of Retinoic acid receptor alpha. These compounds—Pentane, Phorbaketal A, and Ailanthoidol—share a common mechanism of action, likely involving the activation of Retinoic acid receptor alpha, which in turn influences the activity of DNA polymerase alpha subunit B. The evidence suggests that the compound may function as a ligand or activator of Retinoic acid receptor alpha, thereby modulating DNA polymerase alpha subunit B activity. The consistent targeting of DNA polymerase alpha subunit B across these pathways implies a potential role for the compound in regulating DNA replication or repair processes, though the exact mechanism of interaction remains to be fully elucidated.",
